{"id":"leetcode-1025","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Divisor Game","summary":"Alice and Bob play a game starting with a number n.","statement":"Alice and Bob play a game starting with a number n. Alice begins. Each player, on their turn, selects an integer x such that 0 < x < n and n is divisible by x, then replaces n with n - x. The player who cannot make a move loses. Determine if Alice wins under optimal play.","constraints":["Players choose a proper positive divisor and subtract it; no move loses.","Return whether Alice wins with optimal play."],"topics":["dynamic-programming","math"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"alice_wins_divisor_game","parameters":[{"name":"n","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"bool","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def alice_wins_divisor_game(n: int) -> bool:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def alice_wins_divisor_game(n):\n return n%2==0\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def alice_wins_divisor_game(n):\n return n%2==1\n","def alice_wins_divisor_game(n):\n return n>1\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(1)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Experimenting with the game reveals parity is the complete state invariant.","Even n can subtract one and hand over odd; every divisor of odd n is odd, leaving even.","Return true exactly when n is even.","Induction makes odd positions losing and even positions winning from the base n=1."],"editorial":"Induction makes odd positions losing and even positions winning from the base n=1.","tests":[{"id":"lc-1025-1","arguments":[2],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Alice subtracts one and leaves one, so she wins.","expected_n